==District 2==
{{see also|North Carolina's 2nd congressional district}}
The incumbent is Republican [[George Holding]], who has represented the district since 2017. Holding was elected with 57% of the vote in 2016.

The [[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]] included North Carolina's 2nd congressional district on its initial list of Republican-held seats considered targets in 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.politico.com/story/2017/01/dccc-2018-targets-234366|title=Amid Democratic doldrums, DCCC identifies 2018 targets|work=[[Politico]]|last=Cheney|first=Kyle|date=January 30, 2017|accessdate=February 11, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://action.dccc.org/pdf/dccc-on-offense.pdf|title=House Democrats Playing Offense|work=[[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]]|last=Sena|first=Dan|date=January 30, 2017|accessdate=February 11, 2017}}</ref>

